# Forgot Password Button Troubleshooting

## Task List
- [x] Go to http://localhost:3000/login
- [x] Inspect the "Forgot Password?" button area using DOM tool
- [x] Check for overlapping elements or z-index issues
- [x] Click the button and check console logs
- [x] Capture a screenshot with the button highlighted
- [x] Report findings

## Findings
- The button is element [5] in the DOM at (577, 608) scaled / (1108, 585) CSS.
- **Overlays:** No elements are overlapping the button. `elementFromPoint` correctly returns the `BUTTON` at all corners and center.
- **Background Blobs:** Several background decoration elements exist (blur-3xl) but all have `pointer-events: none`.
- **Functionality:** Clicking the button (via pixel click or JS `.click()`) does NOT trigger any navigation or console errors.
- **Comparison:** The "Register" button (right below it) works perfectly and navigates correctly.
- **UI/UX:** The "Forgot Password?" button is very small (10px height, no padding) and lacks a proper `href` or working click handler in the React code.
- **Next steps:** The issue is likely a code-level bug (missing/broken event handler) rather than a CSS/overlay issue.
